A||||5||RedRavenGT||Need help with charging system....||||8||
Z||000000||RedRavenGT||09-23-2001||07:25 PM||||Heres my problem....<P>Had replaced my alternator a few months ago. The cars guage then showed low voltage and the volt light came on.....replaced the alternator. Problem solved. (was a new battery also).<P>About a week ago, my guage started to drop and showed around 12 or 11 for awhile until last night and the car totally died. So I thought it was the alternator and replaced that again today.....didnt work.....so I figured the battery.....didnt work either...car shows 12.8 volts running or not...because of the new battery.<P>I know the alt is good because I had the guy test it before I left the store.....<P>Any ideas on what to do or where to start?<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>(formerly known as V8Fiero)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redraven.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||09-23-2001||07:41 PM||||Hey Scott!<BR>Start with a volt meter and check the BATT terminal on the alt, it should show +12 volts to ground...<BR>Then pull the plug out of the alt. It should have no voltage on either terminal till you turn on the ignition, then +12 volts should be on both...<BR>If the voltage is missing from the Batt terminal, check down at the starter terminal for broken, burnt wires...<BR>If the plug is missing voltage, then I would check at the ignition switch...<BR>hope this helps!<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||09-23-2001||07:48 PM||||A loose belt will also give the symptoms you describe.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RedRavenGT||09-23-2001||08:04 PM||||Ok. I just checked the voltages Fierowrecker.<BR>Ive got 12.5 at the BAT terminal and 7.? at the plug.<P>Now where would you suggest? The ignition switch in the dash? or on the starter?<P>Scot||||reg||1
Z||000004||RedRavenGT||09-23-2001||08:32 PM||||Rechecked all voltages and they were ok. I did bend one of the tabs on the alt when I put the plug in. That turned off the voltage light and now it shows charging at 12.5 volts. Im gonna replace the belt tomorrow. It does look a little worn. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||09-23-2001||08:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RedRavenGT:<BR><B>Rechecked all voltages and they were ok. I did bend one of the tabs on the alt when I put the plug in. That turned off the voltage light and now it shows charging at 12.5 volts. Im gonna replace the belt tomorrow. It does look a little worn. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, hopefully, you got it!<BR>Now you need to use an ampmeter to see if it is putting out enough current...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
